---
import SiteLayout from '../../layouts/SiteLayout.astro';
---

<SiteLayout
  title="Command-Line Launching | ArcadeDuck"
  description="Launch ArcadeDuck from the command line, cabinet frontends, and scripts, including split and merged ROM-set clone launching."
>
  <section class="page-hero command-line-hero">
    <p class="eyebrow">Documentation</p>
    <h1>Command-line launching</h1>
    <p class="page-description">
      Launch arcade sets directly from Windows, cabinet frontends, shortcuts,
      or scripts. ArcadeDuck supports non-merged, split, and merged ROM layouts,
      including selecting logical clones from merged collections.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="systems-status-section command-line-docs">
    <div class="systems-group-heading">
      <div>
        <p class="eyebrow">Quick Start</p>
        <h2>Launch a set directly</h2>
      </div>
      <p>
        The boot filename must be a recognized ArcadeDuck ZIP archive. Quote
        Windows paths when they contain spaces.
      </p>
    </div>

    <pre><code>ArcadeDuck.exe "D:\Arcade\roms\tekken.zip"</code></pre>

    <p>
      For a cabinet or external frontend, <code>-nogui</code> suppresses the
      main ArcadeDuck window and exits when emulation shuts down.
      <code>-fullscreen</code> starts the game in fullscreen.
    </p>

    <pre><code>ArcadeDuck.exe -nogui -fullscreen "D:\Arcade\roms\tekken.zip"</code></pre>
  </section>

  <section class="systems-status-section command-line-docs">
    <div class="systems-group-heading">
      <div>
        <p class="eyebrow">ROM Sets</p>
        <h2>Non-merged, split, and merged layouts</h2>
      </div>
      <p>
        ArcadeDuck's database describes complete logical game sets and resolves
        those definitions from non-merged, split, or merged physical ZIP
        layouts.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="planned-system-grid">
      <article class="planned-system-card">
        <span class="hardware-manufacturer">Non-Merged</span>
        <h3>Launch the game's ZIP</h3>
        <p>A complete set has its own archive. Launch that archive directly.</p>
        <pre><code>ArcadeDuck.exe "D:\Arcade\roms\tekkenac.zip"</code></pre>
      </article>

      <article class="planned-system-card">
        <span class="hardware-manufacturer">Split</span>
        <h3>Clone plus parent archives</h3>
        <p>
          A clone ZIP may contain only clone-specific ROMs. ArcadeDuck searches
          the clone and its parent chain, including matching sibling archives
          in the same ROM directory and indexed archives.
        </p>
        <pre><code>ArcadeDuck.exe "D:\Arcade\roms\tekkenac.zip"</code></pre>
      </article>

      <article class="planned-system-card">
        <span class="hardware-manufacturer">Merged</span>
        <h3>Select the logical clone</h3>
        <p>
          Launch the physical parent ZIP and use <code>-arcadegame</code> to
          select the clone definition stored inside the merged collection.
        </p>
        <pre><code>ArcadeDuck.exe "D:\Arcade\roms\tekken.zip" -arcadegame tekkenac</code></pre>
      </article>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="systems-status-section command-line-docs">
    <div class="systems-group-heading">
      <div>
        <p class="eyebrow">Merged Clone Example</p>
        <h2>What <code>-arcadegame</code> means</h2>
      </div>
    </div>

    <pre><code>ArcadeDuck.exe -nogui -fullscreen "D:\Arcade\roms\tekken.zip" -arcadegame tekkenac</code></pre>

    <p>
      In this command, <code>tekken.zip</code> is the physical archive being
      opened and <code>tekkenac</code> is the logical ArcadeDuck game ID to
      boot. The requested ID must exist in ArcadeDuck's arcade database and
      must be the archive's own set or a descendant of that set.
    </p>

    <p>
      ArcadeDuck scans ZIP members by ROM metadata and accepts matching members
      stored in subdirectories inside a merged archive. For split layouts, it
      also searches the selected game's parent archive chain.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="systems-status-section command-line-docs">
    <div class="systems-group-heading">
      <div>
        <p class="eyebrow">ROM Resolution</p>
        <h2>One resolver for supported arcade systems</h2>
      </div>
      <p>
        Non-merged, split, and merged ROM handling is part of ArcadeDuck's
        standard arcade ROM resolver. There is no separate ROM-set type setting;
        ArcadeDuck uses the game's database definition and parent lineage to find
        the required ROMs from the archives that are present.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="systems-status-section command-line-docs">
    <div class="systems-group-heading">
      <div>
        <p class="eyebrow">Common Launches</p>
        <h2>Ready-to-use examples</h2>
      </div>
    </div>

    <pre><code># Normal direct launch
ArcadeDuck.exe "D:\Arcade\roms\tekken.zip"

# Fullscreen launch
ArcadeDuck.exe -fullscreen "D:\Arcade\roms\tekken.zip"

# Cabinet/frontend launch with no main ArcadeDuck window
ArcadeDuck.exe -nogui -fullscreen "D:\Arcade\roms\tekken.zip"

# Launch a clone from a merged parent archive
ArcadeDuck.exe -nogui -fullscreen "D:\Arcade\roms\tekken.zip" -arcadegame tekkenac

# Use a separate settings file
ArcadeDuck.exe -settings "cabinet.ini" "D:\Arcade\roms\tekken.zip"

# Show the built-in command-line help
ArcadeDuck.exe -help</code></pre>
  </section>

  <section class="systems-status-section command-line-docs">
    <div class="systems-group-heading">
      <div>
        <p class="eyebrow">Option Reference</p>
        <h2>Public command-line options</h2>
      </div>
      <p>
        <code>ArcadeDuck.exe -help</code> is the built-in reference shipped
        with the executable.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="command-option-table-wrapper">
      <table class="command-option-table">
        <thead>
          <tr><th>Option</th><th>Behavior</th></tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr><td><code>-help</code></td><td>Displays command-line help and exits.</td></tr>
          <tr><td><code>-version</code></td><td>Displays version information and exits.</td></tr>
          <tr><td><code>-arcadegame &lt;id&gt;</code></td><td>Selects the logical arcade game to launch from the supplied archive, including clones from split or merged sets.</td></tr>
          <tr><td><code>-fullscreen</code></td><td>Enters fullscreen mode immediately after starting.</td></tr>
          <tr><td><code>-nofullscreen</code></td><td>Prevents fullscreen mode from triggering when it would otherwise be enabled.</td></tr>
          <tr><td><code>-nogui</code></td><td>Suppresses the main window and exits when the emulated system shuts down.</td></tr>
          <tr><td><code>-settings &lt;filename&gt;</code></td><td>Loads a custom settings configuration; default settings are used if the file does not exist.</td></tr>
          <tr><td><code>-earlyconsole</code></td><td>Creates the console as early as possible for logging.</td></tr>
          <tr><td><code>--</code></td><td>Stops option parsing so the remaining arguments are treated as the boot filename.</td></tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="systems-note">
    <div>
      <p class="eyebrow">Paths</p>
      <h2>Quote Windows paths containing spaces.</h2>
    </div>
    <p>
      Use <code>--</code> when you need to explicitly end option parsing,
      especially when a boot filename could begin with a dash. The boot archive
      itself must exist and be recognized by ArcadeDuck's arcade database.
    </p>
  </section>

  <style>
    .command-line-hero { max-width: 940px; }

    .command-line-docs > p {
      max-width: 900px;
      color: var(--text-muted);
      line-height: 1.7;
    }

    .command-line-docs pre {
      overflow-x: auto;
      margin: 22px 0;
      padding: 20px 22px;
      border: 1px solid var(--border);
      border-radius: 10px;
      background: rgba(18, 16, 28, 0.78);
    }

    .command-line-docs pre code {
      color: #d9c8ff;
      font-family: ui-monospace, SFMono-Regular, Consolas, monospace;
      font-size: 0.88rem;
      line-height: 1.65;
    }

    .command-line-docs .planned-system-card pre {
      margin-bottom: 0;
      padding: 15px 16px;
      white-space: pre-wrap;
      overflow-wrap: anywhere;
    }

    .command-line-tags { gap: 10px; }

    .command-option-table-wrapper {
      overflow-x: auto;
      border: 1px solid var(--border);
      border-radius: 12px;
    }

    .command-option-table {
      width: 100%;
      min-width: 760px;
      border-collapse: collapse;
      background: rgba(18, 16, 28, 0.68);
    }

    .command-option-table th {
      padding: 15px 18px;
      color: var(--text-muted);
      background: rgba(156, 92, 255, 0.055);
      font-size: 0.72rem;
      font-weight: 800;
      letter-spacing: 0.07em;
      text-align: left;
      text-transform: uppercase;
    }

    .command-option-table td {
      padding: 17px 18px;
      border-top: 1px solid var(--border);
      color: var(--text-muted);
      line-height: 1.55;
      vertical-align: top;
    }

    .command-option-table td:first-child {
      width: 220px;
      white-space: nowrap;
    }

    .command-option-table code,
    .systems-note code,
    .command-line-docs p code {
      color: #d9c8ff;
      font-family: ui-monospace, SFMono-Regular, Consolas, monospace;
    }
  </style>
</SiteLayout>
